        <summary>A free, powerful, multi-purpose tool that helps you monitor system resources, debug software and detect malware.</summary>
        <description># System Informer

A free, powerful, multi-purpose tool that helps you monitor system resources, debug software and detect malware. Formerly known as Process Hacker. Brought to you by Winsider Seminars &amp; Solutions, Inc.

## System Requirements

Windows 10 or higher, 32-bit, 64-bit, or ARM64.

## Features

- A detailed overview of system activity with highlighting.
- Graphs and statistics allow you to quickly track down resource hogs and runaway processes.
- Can't edit or delete a file? Discover which processes are using that file.
- See what programs have active network connections, and close them if necessary.
- Get real-time information on disk access.
- View detailed stack traces with kernel-mode, WOW64 and .NET support.
- Go beyond services.msc: create, edit and control services.
- 100% [Free Software](https://www.gnu.org/philosophy/free-sw.en.html) ([MIT](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT))

## Antivirus False Positives

System Informer includes a kernel driver and can inspect and terminate other processes, so some antivirus engines flag it. These detections are false positives. The installer is signed by Winsider Seminars &amp; Solutions Inc. and the software is open source. See the developer discussion:

- [Avast detects the driver as vulnerable (#1908)](https://github.com/winsiderss/systeminformer/issues/1908)
- [Windows Defender flagged as a virus and crashed (#1722)](https://github.com/winsiderss/systeminformer/issues/1722)
- [Antivirus false alarms: can we fight them? (#1715)](https://github.com/winsiderss/systeminformer/issues/1715)
- [Flagged as a Potentially Unwanted Application (#1668)](https://github.com/winsiderss/systeminformer/issues/1668)
- [Trojan:Win32/Sabsik.TE.B!ml detected by Windows Defender (#1665)](https://github.com/winsiderss/systeminformer/issues/1665)

## Notes

- The application is not started after installation.
- This package tracks the stable release channel published at [systeminformer.com/downloads](https://systeminformer.com/downloads), not the canary builds.</description>
